    <http://example.org/node/chunk139> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client expects a solution that provides response times compatible with daily clinical use (below 2 seconds for common queries), integrates with existing hospital information systems (SIH) and electronic patient records (DPI), supports health interoperability standards (HL7/FHIR), and includes API-type interfaces." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message6> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk14> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must assist staff in analysing and handling dossiers by surfacing relevant information, recalling applicable rules, and suggesting actions or verifications." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk140> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our current technology stack, performance benchmarks, sovereign hosting options, and technical constraints as of 2024, what is the proposed technical architecture for this solution? the proposed technical architecture for this solution leverages the Atelier platform, a Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) platform, which meets the client's expectations. the Atelier platform, a Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) platform, which meets the client's expectations will be hosted on the Sovereign HDS tier provided by OuraneCloud, ensuring SecNumCloud-qualified, HDS-certified, and EU-only hosting with renewable power. the Atelier platform, a Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) platform, which meets the client's expectations components, including document-ingestion pipeline, vector store, retrieval layer, orchestration layer, and answer layer, will provide the necessary functionality for daily clinical use. the Atelier platform, a Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) platform, which meets the client's expectations model-agnostic design allows for the integration of suitable models, such as our Sovereign European open-weight model, which provides strong grounding and citation behavior." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message6> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk141> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For integration with existing hospital information systems (SIH) and electronic patient records (DPI), our will utilize standard connectors and custom adapters where needed." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message6> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk142> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, our API-first approach with REST and webhook interfaces ensures seamless embedding in existing work environments." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message6> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk143> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To support health interoperability standards, the proposed technical architecture for this solution includes production-ready FHIR/HL7 connectors for main resources, with extended resource coverage on the roadmap. our partnership with Ligeo Santé facilitates delivery and alignment with Ségur / Mon espace santé–DMP frameworks." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message6> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk144> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of performance, our benchmarks indicate that common single-document queries will be below 2 seconds at p95 latency, meeting the client's expectations for response times compatible with daily clinical use. the Atelier platform, a Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) platform, which meets the client's expectations scales horizontally with additional inference capacity to ensure high throughput." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message6> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk145> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Lastly, the proposed technical architecture for this solution includes built-in monitoring, logging, and observability features, supporting 24/7 operation and a 99.9% availability target on the appropriate hosting tier." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message6> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk146> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires strict GDPR compliance, personal and health data protection, medical confidentiality preservation, and data hosting exclusively within the European Union." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message8> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk147> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The infrastructure must hold French Hébergeur de Données de Santé (HDS) certification, and sensitive data must be protected with encryption and pseudonymisation where relevant." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message8> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk148> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our company's certifications, GDPR instruments, AI security controls, audit capabilities, and experience with the European Union regulatory frameworks as of 2024, what are the key security and compliance measures our company's should implement to meet these requirements?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message8> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk149> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To meet The client requirements, our company's will leverage our company's existing ISO 27001 certification, which covers development, delivery, and operations, and our company's ISO 27701 certification for privacy information management. our company's hosting partner, OuraneCloud, is SecNumCloud-qualified and holds HDS certification, ensuring compliance with French health data hosting regulations.  our company's will implement encryption in transit using TLS 1.3 and encryption at rest using AES-256, with key management handled through our company's the European Union infrastructure." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message8> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk15> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must support medical coding (PMSI / ICD-10) for activity reporting (T2A)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk150> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Pseudonymisation will be applied where relevant to protect sensitive data. our company's platform ensures strict isolation between client corpora, with per-engagement logical separation, and role-based access control (RBAC) to restrict access to authorized personnel. our company's will maintain a data processing register, have appointed a Data Protection Officer (DPO), and ensure that our company's Data Processing Agreement (DPA) is aligned with GDPR Article 28. our company's secure software development lifecycle (SDLC) includes code review, dependency scanning, secrets management, and periodic penetration testing by an external CREST-equivalent provider." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message8> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk151> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Incident response procedures are in place, with defined detection, notification, and remediation steps, and a breach notification delay of 72 hours." ;
