    <http://example.org/node/chunk152> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Segregation of duties is implemented between development and production operations to prevent unauthorized access or changes. our company's experience delivering GDPR-compliant solutions to public-sector and health clients, including those involving special-category health data, will be leveraged to ensure compliance with relevant the European Union regulatory frameworks, such as CNIL guidance, HDS reference framework, and HAS guidance on AI in healthcare. our company's product, Atelier, supports explainability, human oversight, source traceability, audit logging, and medical confidentiality preservation, ensuring that all requirements for strict GDPR compliance, personal and health data protection, and medical confidentiality are met." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message8> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk153> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client expects the solution to be designed as an assistance tool, with no clinical or medico-administrative decision automated without explicit validation by a qualified professional. the solution must not require medical-device qualification (CE marking / MDR), and any use case approaching medical-device qualification (CE marking / MDR) must be explicitly addressed." ;
